Identify the historical period and context in which the system of civil services was introduced in India
The system of civil services was introduced in India during the British colonial period, specifically in 1854, when the British government established the Indian Civil Service (ICS) under the Charter Act of 1853. This marked the beginning of a professional bureaucracy in India, which was modeled after the British civil service system.
