According to the provided context, the origin story of Wonder Woman in DC Comics is as follows:

Steve Trevor, an intelligence officer in the United States Army, crashed his plane on Paradise Island, the Amazons' isolated homeland. Princess Diana, the youngest, strongest, and most human of the Amazons, nursed him back to health using a "Purple Ray" and fell in love with him. When the goddess Aphrodite declared that it was time for an Amazon to travel to "Man's World" and fight the evil of the Nazis, a tournament was held to determine who would be the Amazon champion. Princess Diana participated in the tournament, although forbidden by her mother Queen Hippolyte, and was chosen to be the Amazon champion, thus becoming Wonder Woman.
