As of January 7, 2016, the West Indian manatee is proposed to be downlisted from endangered to threatened status under the Endangered Species Act (ESA). However, the proposal to downlist the manatee to threatened will not affect federal protections currently afforded by the ESA. The species was previously listed as endangered in 2013, which is equivalent to the International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN) category of "critically endangered." In 2007, the US Fish and Wildlife Service advised the species be reclassified as threatened rather than endangered.
