Based on general knowledge, to win a Premier League medal, a team must finish at the top of the Premier League table at the end of the season. The requirements are:

1. The team must be an English football club.
2. The team must play a minimum number of games (typically 38) in the Premier League season.
3. The team must earn more points than any other team in the league.

As for the number of games played in a Premier League season, it is typically 38 games per team, with each team playing every other team in the league once at home and once away.
