What is the title and plot of the movie V for Vendetta, and what is the significance of the character V?
The movie "V for Vendetta" is a 2005 live-action film based on the comic book series of the same name. The plot revolves around a dystopian United Kingdom where a totalitarian government, known as the Norsefire regime, has taken control. The title character V, a mysterious anarchist, vigilante, and freedom fighter, seeks to topple the government through acts of heroism. He is easily recognizable by his Guy Fawkes mask, long hair, and dark clothing.

The significance of the character V lies in his moral ambiguity, designed by creator Alan Moore to be a complex figure that readers or viewers can interpret as either a hero fighting for a cause or simply insane. V's actions are driven by his desire to bring down the oppressive government and restore freedom to the people. The film's portrayal of V has become iconic, with the Guy Fawkes mask becoming a symbol of anti-establishment protest worldwide.
