What is the historical context and significance of the song 'Where Have All the Flowers Gone'?
The song "Where Have All the Flowers Gone?" has a historical context and significance as an anti-war protest song. It was written by Pete Seeger and was popularized during the Vietnam War era. The song's lyrics express a sense of loss and longing for a time when wars and violence did not exist, and it has been interpreted as a commentary on the devastating effects of war on society. The song has been covered by many artists, including Merry Hell, Imphal Talkies and The Howlers, and has become an iconic representation of the anti-war movement.
