How did the city of Honolulu transition from being the capital of the Kingdom of Hawaii to becoming the capital of the State of Hawaii after its annexation by the United States?
After the overthrow of the Kingdom of Hawaii in 1893, the city of Honolulu remained the capital of the newly established Republic of Hawaii. When the United States annexed Hawaii in 1898, Honolulu continued to serve as the capital. When Hawaii became a state in 1959, Honolulu remained the capital of the State of Hawaii, having already been the capital of the territory since the annexation.
