Venkaiah Naidu is a senior politician from the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP), which is the party in power in India. He was elected as the Vice President of India in the 2017 Indian vice-presidential election and took oath as the 13th Vice President of India on August 11, 2017.

As for his qualifications and background, Venkaiah Naidu is a seasoned politician with a long career in public service. He was born on July 1, 1949, in Andhra Pradesh, India. He holds a degree in law and has been involved in politics since the 1970s. He has served as a Member of Parliament (MP) in the Lok Sabha and the Rajya Sabha, and has held various ministerial positions in the government of India, including the Ministry of Urban Development and the Ministry of Parliamentary Affairs.

Venkaiah Naidu is known for his strong leadership skills, his commitment to public service, and his ability to work across party lines. He has been a key figure in the BJP and has played a significant role in shaping the party's policies and strategies. As the Vice President of India and the Chairman of the Rajya Sabha, he is expected to play a crucial role in promoting the interests of the country and the parliament.
