What are the current start and end dates of daylight saving time in the United States, and have there been any recent changes or proposals to modify these dates?
Based on the provided context, the current start date of daylight saving time in the United States is the second Sunday in March, and the current end date is the first Sunday in November. 

There have been changes to these dates in the past. Prior to 2007, the start date was the first Sunday in April, and the end date was the last Sunday in October. The Energy Policy Act of 2005 extended daylight saving time, starting in 2007, by moving the start date to the second Sunday in March and keeping the end date as the first Sunday in November. 

There is no mention of recent changes or proposals to modify these dates in the provided context.
