What was the historical event or series of events that led to the forced relocation of the Cherokee Nation from their ancestral lands to the west?
The historical event that led to the forced relocation of the Cherokee Nation from their ancestral lands to the west is known as the Trail of Tears. It was a series of events and policies implemented by the United States government, particularly the Indian Removal Act of 1830 signed by President Andrew Jackson, which led to the forced relocation of the Cherokee Nation from their ancestral lands in Georgia, North Carolina, and Tennessee to Indian Territory (present-day Oklahoma) in the 1830s.
