Based on the provided context, the muscles that attach to the scapula and have a medial attachment point are:

* Trapezius (attaches to the medial border of the scapula)
* Levator scapulae (attaches to the medial border of the scapula)
* Rhomboid muscles (attach to the medial, superior, and inferior borders of the scapula)
* Serratus anterior (attaches to the medial border of the scapula)

The muscles that do not have a medial attachment point are:

* Biceps (attaches to the coracoid process and supraglenoid tubercle of the scapula)
* Triceps (attaches to the infraglenoid tubercle of the scapula)
* Deltoid (attaches to the coracoid process and supraglenoid tubercle of the scapula)
* Subscapularis (attaches to the surface of the scapula)
* Infraspinatus (attaches to the surface of the scapula)
* Teres minor (attaches to the surface of the scapula)
* Supraspinatus (attaches to the surface of the scapula)
